            {
                "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                "word": "switchblade",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e79a76a4-ecdc-4863-b51a-d03d142b3e6f",
                        "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "switchblades"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "59e989ca-0b5a-4a3e-8b43-805d3a0e825d",
                        "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "switchblading"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "6305a57e-6639-4552-8279-5c7dbbe9490f",
                        "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "switchbladed"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "a8e052c6-6289-4549-b7b7-cddf6ad704f8",
                        "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "switchbladed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8a5da6e8-5acd-3c86-b0fa-471f77b22297",
                        "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To attack or cut with a switchblade."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab8d163f-51fd-4221-8788-95e1c84e5c44",
                                "sense_id": "8a5da6e8-5acd-3c86-b0fa-471f77b22297",
                                "text": "I got terrible hangovers from the cheap booze; and, one night, I almost got switchbladed when I put my arm around the wrong \"lady of the night."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8a58343-efbf-4f4f-9735-9d34f536ce62",
                                "sense_id": "8a5da6e8-5acd-3c86-b0fa-471f77b22297",
                                "text": "They are the American dream torn asunder, like clean fresh laundry left drying on the clothesline, switchbladed by bored boys of summer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b857173-dbb3-4e92-a2bc-af09de63a539",
                                "sense_id": "8a5da6e8-5acd-3c86-b0fa-471f77b22297",
                                "text": "Finally there was Jackie, the gold-toothed gang member (as she liked to remind us) who'd switchbladed thirty or forty or fifty people"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "76f442c3-a070-3586-af87-cbbed7116c2d",
                        "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To spring open or up."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02bd4d20-c17a-49fa-ba07-4bfb8ed2894f",
                                "sense_id": "76f442c3-a070-3586-af87-cbbed7116c2d",
                                "text": "Switchblading open their silvery cell phones, they call their mortgage brokers and say “Buy.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e411952c-6ec9-47a0-88cd-71adb96fc1b1",
                                "sense_id": "76f442c3-a070-3586-af87-cbbed7116c2d",
                                "text": "Steering and stabilization fins switchblading out, followed by the wings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fb87843-2e1a-4612-b3eb-27f0c8acb3de",
                                "sense_id": "76f442c3-a070-3586-af87-cbbed7116c2d",
                                "text": "I stood there waiting for the three remaining Rottweilers to come barreling toward the fence, fangs switchbladed open."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a73ae533-8672-48df-b57e-5a34674ed587",
                                "sense_id": "76f442c3-a070-3586-af87-cbbed7116c2d",
                                "text": "He ticked off the facts, switchblading out a finger for each one."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9df25b9f-934a-3e43-8c22-221f6728333a",
                        "entry_id": "754133dd-ef6c-3514-b804-1a648011ab07",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To (cause to) make a sudden move or transition."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "25e27887-533d-48ca-94bc-cd4a5b5223a7",
                                "sense_id": "9df25b9f-934a-3e43-8c22-221f6728333a",
                                "text": "He briefly rocked medical school, switchbladed to accounting and finally joked his first radio script in 1938."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7161186-c967-4496-a7dc-637e40bed2d1",
                                "sense_id": "9df25b9f-934a-3e43-8c22-221f6728333a",
                                "text": "The play's principal comic manoeuvre is to have concern switchblading into callousness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cb23b12-a296-4c14-93c7-e4d0f94450d4",
                                "sense_id": "9df25b9f-934a-3e43-8c22-221f6728333a",
                                "text": "Daniel's smile is fixed, but his eyes are switchblading from side to side, looking at Paula, looking for an exit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a8d4439-8804-457a-8944-dd1cd95a94a6",
                                "sense_id": "9df25b9f-934a-3e43-8c22-221f6728333a",
                                "text": "The lantern began swinging to its own rhythm, switchblading light all over the tent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
